	"ResourceName": "okta_user_denylist",
	"Description": "Escalate Okta alerts for an account (actor or person acted on) to at least High.\n\nColumns: key,enabled,min_risk,reason\nKey: \u003clogin\u003e|\u003cdetection name\u003e or \u003clogin\u003e|*. min_risk (optional): only escalate when the risk score is at least this value; empty or 0 = always. This raises the priority of alerts a detection already produced; it does not create alerts.\n\nThe detection name is the scheduled search name after the group, e.g. \"Okta Admin Console Access from a New IP\". Logins are lowercase and without @domain. Rows with enabled = 0 are ignored; the shipped rows are disabled examples. Used by every Okta detection and the modification feed through $OKTA_USER_TUNING / $OKTA_IP_TUNING.",
